From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shigeaki Asai <y-asai.0816@docomonet.jp>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 11:04:17 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] arm: dts: meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra-u-boot: limit the
 eMMC to 26MHz

After a cold boot, U-Boot often cannot read the eMMC on the ODROID-GO
Ultra (Samsung AJTD4R). In the high speed mode at 40MHz the 8-bit bus
test fails, U-Boot falls back to a 1-bit bus, and reads then fail, so
distro boot finds no partition table on mmc 1 and the board cannot boot
from the eMMC. With a UART cable attached it failed on most cold boots.

Limit the eMMC to 26MHz in U-Boot. This needs the previous patch, which
makes the meson MMC driver use a lower max-frequency from the device
tree; without it the property is ignored. With both, mmc info shows an
8-bit bus at 26MHz, and the board booted from the eMMC on 80 of 80 boots
(60 cold, 20 warm, with and without a UART cable and a microSD card).
Linux is not affected.

This patch was written with the help of Claude (claude-opus-5-5).

Signed-off-by: Shigeaki Asai <y-asai.0816@docomonet.jp>
---
 arch/arm/dts/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra-u-boot.dtsi | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra-u-boot.dtsi b/arch/arm/dts/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra-u-boot.dtsi
index 9ae0a50..a8a7693 100644
--- a/arch/arm/dts/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra-u-boot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -30,3 +30,13 @@
 &vddio_c {
 	regulator-init-microvolt = <3300000>;
 };
+
+/*
+ * After a cold boot, U-Boot sometimes cannot use the eMMC in the high speed
+ * mode at 40MHz: the 8-bit bus test fails, it falls back to a 1-bit bus, and
+ * reads then fail, so the board cannot boot from the eMMC. This controller
+ * has no tuning in U-Boot; at 26MHz the 8-bit bus works.
+ */
+&sd_emmc_c {
+	max-frequency = <26000000>;
+};
